180
00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:42.032
when combined with time and venue. No
product approval, retention

181
00:18:42.032 --> 00:18:46.904
term, or tested model behavior is
asserted. Mandatory pre-action approval

182
00:18:46.904 --> 00:18:51.776
is distinct from quality auditing. Every
proposed assignment must receive

183
00:18:51.776 --> 00:18:56.648
coordinator approval before it is
communicated, published, or used. A

184
00:18:56.648 --> 00:19:01.520
later quality audit is a separate check
performed on a

185
00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:06.392
defined sample of eligible completed
assignments. Auditing never substitutes

186
00:19:06.392 --> 00:19:11.264
for the 100 percent pre-action approval
requirement. Controls include redaction

187
00:19:11.264 --> 00:19:16.136
before entry, an approved account and
workspace, least-privilege access, no

188
00:19:16.136 --> 00:19:21.008
messaging or record-editing tools, fixed
role and availability fields, and

189
00:19:21.008 --> 00:19:25.880
mandatory human approval. Detection
includes comparing every draft assignment

190
00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:30.752
with the source roster before approval,
recording the reviewer and

191
00:19:30.752 --> 00:19:35.624
decision, logging the prompt version, and
collecting volunteer corrections. Recovery

192
00:19:35.624 --> 00:19:40.496
is owned by the coordinator: pause
publication, review the prompt,

193
00:19:40.496 --> 00:19:45.368
output, access log, and source roster,
correct the assignment or

194
00:19:45.368 --> 00:19:50.240
roster, notify affected volunteers, revoke
access and escalate if prohibited

195
00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:55.112
data was exposed, and restore the last
approved manual roster.

196
00:19:55.112 --> 00:19:59.984
The operations director owns retirement
approval. This fictional worked plan

197
00:19:59.984 --> 00:20:04.856
covers only internal draft assignments for
Riverbend Repair Day on

198
00:20:04.856 --> 00:20:09.728
2026-10-17. The volunteer coordinator owns
approval, monitoring, correction, incident

199
00:20:09.728 --> 00:20:14.600
response, and recovery. Monitoring uses
the fixed event window from

200
00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:19.472
2026-10-03 through 2026-10-31, inclusive.
The coordinator records the actual

201
00:20:19.472 --> 00:20:24.344
observation counts, numerator,
denominator, and window dates. No

202
00:20:24.344 --> 00:20:29.216
observation or count is asserted here.
Every proposed assignment requires

203
00:20:29.216 --> 00:20:34.088
documented coordinator approval before it
is communicated, published, or used.

204
00:20:34.088 --> 00:20:38.960
The pre-action approval metric is separate
from quality auditing: numerator

205
00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:43.832
is the number of proposed assignments with
approval recorded before

206
00:20:43.832 --> 00:20:48.704
the action; denominator is all proposed
assignments in the monitoring

207
00:20:48.704 --> 00:20:53.576
window; threshold is 100 percent. A
quality audit cannot substitute

208
00:20:53.576 --> 00:20:58.448
for this requirement. Any missing approval
triggers an immediate pause,

209
00:20:58.448 --> 00:21:03.320
prevents communication or use of the
affected assignment, and requires

210
00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:08.192
the coordinator to review the source
roster, prompt, output, and

211
00:21:08.192 --> 00:21:13.064
access log before deciding whether to
correct, notify, revoke access,

212
00:21:13.064 --> 00:21:17.936
or restore the approved manual roster.
Unsupported-assignment rate is measured

213
00:21:17.936 --> 00:21:22.808
over the fixed event window. Numerator is
the number of

214
00:21:22.808 --> 00:21:27.680
approved assignments containing at least
one assignment claim not supported

215
00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:32.552
by the permitted roster fields or event
records. Denominator is

216
00:21:32.552 --> 00:21:37.424
all eligible assignments that were
actually approved and reviewed during

217
00:21:37.424 --> 00:21:42.296
the window. An eligible assignment is one
that reached the

218
00:21:42.296 --> 00:21:47.168
relevant event in scope and had a recorded
assignment outcome

219
00:21:47.168 --> 00:21:52.040
during the window. Threshold is 0 percent.
Any unsupported assignment

220
00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:56.912
triggers an immediate pause. The
